<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29828" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῶρον</span></b> , τό, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίδωμι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>gift, present, gift of honour</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγλαὰ δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.213
				</span></i>
			, etc.; <i>votive gift</i> or <i>offering</i> to a god, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φέρε δῶρον Ἀθήνῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					6.293
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ge.</u>
				4.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Marc.</u>
				7.11
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βωμοὶ δώροισι φλέγονται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					91
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποῦ μοι τὰ . . δ.
			κἀκροθίνια</span>; <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				184
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῶρά τινος</span>
			<i>the gifts of</i>, i. e. <i>given by</i>, him, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεῶν ἐρικυδέα δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					20.265
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				18.142
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῶρ᾽ Ἀφροδίτης</span>, i.e.
			personal charms, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				3.54
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				64
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. Κύπριδος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					363
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. τῶν Μουσῶν καὶ
				Ἀπόλλωνος</span>, of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μουσική</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				796e
			</span></i>: c. gen. rei, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕπνου δ.</span>
			<i>the blessing</i> of sleep, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				7.482
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῶρα</span>
			<i>presents</i> given as tribute, <i><span class="en">
				17.225
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῶρον τοῦ ποταμοῦ</span>, of
			the land of Egypt, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῶρα</span>
			<i>presents</i>, as retaining fees or bribes, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				18.109
			</span></i>, Jusj.ib.<i><span class="en">
				24.150
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Ath.</u>
				55.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				953.7
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Calymna</span>), etc. (the usual sense of
			the word in 
				Att.
			 Oratt.): hence in 
				Att.
			 law, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δώρων γραφή</span> an
			indictment <i>for being bribed</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				3.232
			</span></i>, etc., cf. <i><span class="en">
				Harp.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δώρων κριθῆναι</span> to be
			tried <i>for taking bribes</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				27.3
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δώρων ἑλεῖν τινα</span> to
			convict him <i>of taking bribes</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				591
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. ὀφλεῖν</span> to be found
			guilty <i>of taking bribes</i>, <i><span class="en">
				And.
				1.74
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δώρων δίωξις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Per.</u>
					32
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> in pl.,
				<i>good qualities, talents</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ βασιλέως δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lib.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					19
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>front part of palm</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				2.144
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>hand's breadth, palm</i>, as a measure of length, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				398
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Vitr.
				2.3.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Milet.</u>
				7.57
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Didyma</span>); cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεκάδωρος</span>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
